WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.635
Drone-based inspection improves access, documentation, repeatability, and safety when properly planned.

00:00:06.635 --> 00:00:15.394
It supports roofs, bridges, towers, utilities, solar arrays, corridors, industrial sites, facilities, and damage assessment.

00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:24.152
Begin with a bounded inspection question, asset, required detail, constraints, deliverables, specialist needs, and exclusions.

00:00:24.152 --> 00:00:32.911
Plan current rules, permissions, weather, obstacles, standoff, route, crew communication, battery segments, and emergency options.

00:00:32.911 --> 00:00:42.200
Select R G B, zoom, thermal, video, or specialized sensors according to evidence needs and limitations.

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:50.959
Capture stable overview, intermediate, and close-up views with coverage, scale context, metadata, and repeatable routes.

00:00:50.959 --> 00:00:57.594
Organize originals, notes, tags, maps, and reports with traceable evidence references.

00:00:57.594 --> 00:01:06.883
Protect sensitive infrastructure data and state confidence, collection limits, missing coverage, and need for qualified interpretation.

00:01:06.883 --> 00:01:15.111
The goal is useful inspection support, not replacing engineering judgment or forcing unsafe missions.

00:01:15.111 --> 00:01:23.338
Strong programs combine safe flight, disciplined capture, defensible evidence, privacy, security, and specialist review.
